# Test: an announce that names no next hop is refused with its true cause, and
#       the fix names the next-hop form to write.
#
# QUESTION: does an operator who types `send bgp * update text origin igp nlri
# add 10.0.0.0/24` read that the command named no next hop and how to give
# one, rather than a done answer or "no peers have family negotiated"? The unit
# test (TestAnnounceNLRIBatch_NoNextHopNamesTheCause) builds the batch by hand;
# only the real dispatcher proves that ParseUpdateText leaves the next hop
# unset, that AnnounceNLRIBatch refuses it, and that DispatchNLRIGroups hands
# the refusal to the operator as an error rather than downgrading it.
# VALIDATES: announceNextHopMissing
#            (internal/component/bgp/reactor/peer_nexthop_refusal.go) reaches
#            the operator through `send bgp * update text`.
# PREVENTS:  the peer, which is still coming up, queuing a route that can
#            never be sent and the command answering done. Remove the refusal
#            before the peer loop in AnnounceNLRIBatch and the command
#            succeeds, which fails expect=command-error.
#
# The peer never connects (accept false), so it is not established and an
# announce with a next hop is queued and accepted.

stdin=config:terminator=EOF_CONFIG
plugin {
	external engine-steps {
		run "le mock engine-steps ./engine-steps.json"
		encoder json
	}
}

bgp {
	peer peer1 {
		connection {
			remote {
				ip 127.0.0.1
			}
			local {
				ip 127.0.0.1
				accept false
			}
		}
		session {
			asn {
				local 1
				remote 1
			}
			router-id 1.2.3.4
			family {
				ipv4/unicast { prefix { maximum 10000; } }
			}
			capability {
				graceful-restart disable
			}
		}
		attach process engine-steps {
			send [ update ]
		}
	}
}
EOF_CONFIG

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze -:stdin=config:timeout=30s

# The same announce with a next hop is accepted: an announcement refused here
# fails the run, because no expect=command-error consumes it.
command=send bgp * update text origin igp next-hop 10.0.0.1 nlri add 10.0.0.0/24

# Without a next hop it is refused, with the cause and the fix.
command=send bgp * update text origin igp nlri add 10.0.0.0/24
expect=command-error:contains=the announce of ipv4/unicast routes names no next hop
command=send bgp * update text origin igp nlri add 10.0.0.0/24
expect=command-error:contains=fix: update text next-hop <address> or update text next-hop self, before the first nlri or mp section

expect=exit:code=0
expect=stderr:contains=engine-steps: all steps passed
reject=stderr:pattern=panic recovered
reject=stderr:pattern=fatal error
reject=stderr:pattern=no peers have family negotiated
